        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Dr. Lefkowitz work for both plaintiff and defense in Kentucky?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. He reviews Kentucky eye cases for plaintiff and defense counsel, and gives the same independent opinion either way.",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://www.expertophthalmologywitness.com/#todd-lefkowitz"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can he be the consulting expert for a Kentucky certificate of merit?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Under KRS 411.167 the attorney files the certificate of merit with the complaint, stating that a qualified expert was consulted and found a reasonable basis for the claim. Dr. Lefkowitz can review the records and serve as that consulting expert, and he can also provide affidavits.",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://www.expertophthalmologywitness.com/#todd-lefkowitz"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does he need to travel to Kentucky?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not for most of the work. Case review and depositions can be done by phone or video conference. He will travel to Kentucky for trial testimony.",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://www.expertophthalmologywitness.com/#todd-lefkowitz"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How soon should a Kentucky case be sent for review?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "As early as possible. Kentucky generally gives one year from when the injury was discovered, or should have been discovered, to file a medical negligence claim (KRS 413.140). Your counsel should confirm the deadline for your case.",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://www.expertophthalmologywitness.com/#todd-lefkowitz"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
